+## Unsmell run 2026-11-02 (`EventSignatureRow` struct)
+
+- **Event-signature cache key is a data clump.** `src/evm/cache/event_signature_cache.rs`
+  `get_event_signature` and `insert_event_signature` both take `chain_id`,
+  `address` and `event_name` as three parameters, and the adapter in
+  `src/bin/chainfold/signature_cache.rs` (`get` and `put`) builds them the same
+  way twice from the trait's raw `u64`, `[u8; 20]` and `&str`. Fix: an
+  `EventSignatureKey { chain_id: ChainId, address: Address, event_name: &str }`
+  that both methods take, built once per adapter call by a constructor from the
+  raw values.
+- **Module doc of `event_signature_cache.rs` reads back its own name and shape.**
+  Lines 1-8 open with `EventSignatureCache`, restate the row as the tuple
+  `(chain, address, event name) → (signature, topic0, abi)`, and keep a note on
+  why the type was named as it is. Fix: rewrite it as the module's place in the
+  system, for example "Stores the event signatures that the resolver has found,
+  one row per chain, contract and event name, so that a repeated lookup needs no
+  network request." Drop the naming note.
